# Cassandra pods on __CLUSTER_NAME__ cluster

Image: `--image` if given, else `cassandra:<--version>`
Nodes: __CASSANDRA_NODES__ (one pod per db node, DB nodes: __DB_NODE_COUNT__)
Datacenter: __CASSANDRA_DC__, rack `rack1`
Storage per node: __STORAGE_SIZE__
Region: __REGION__

## Connect

CQL listens on port 30942 of every db node IP:

```bash
cqlsh <db-node-ip> 30942
```

## Lifecycle

```bash
easy-db-lab cassandra-pods start
easy-db-lab cassandra-pods stop        # keeps the data volumes
easy-db-lab kit uninstall cassandra-pods   # deletes the data volumes
```

Metrics arrive as `job="cassandra"`, so the Cassandra dashboards show these pods.
